#
# S25 port of testkit's scenarios/alloc-per-request against a REAL cache_turbo
# HIT path (../nginx.conf), not the bare `return 200` the generic conf ships.
#
# WHAT THE GENERIC SCENARIO PROVES, AND WHY IT WAS VACUOUS HERE UNWIRED
#   Upstream's alloc-per-request drives request SIZE (a long line, huge header
#   values, a discarded body) against testkit's own /__probe location and
#   watches nginx's generic pool.cycle_*/fds counters stay flat. Every one of
#   those requests, run against this module's *default* generic conf, would
#   never touch a `cache_turbo` location at all -- a green run would prove
#   nginx itself is allocation-neutral and say nothing about this module's own
#   per-request HIT-path work (cache-key lookup, node refcounting, header
#   replay). That is exactly the "vacuous-green" class testkit.yml's own
#   header documents.
#
# THE FIX: EVERY MEASURED CASE HITS /cached/, NOT /__probe
#   cache_turbo_key in ../nginx.conf is `$uri` (path only, no query string),
#   so every case below -- regardless of how much query-string padding it
#   carries -- addresses the SAME cache entry. driver.sh populates and verifies
#   that entry BEFORE prober takes this run's origin snapshot, so every case is
#   a genuine HIT. The padded-query/padded-header/body cases are therefore
#   size-class stress on cache_turbo's OWN filter chain (HIT-path header replay,
#   refcounted lookup), not on a passthrough.
#
#   zone.slab_* is asserted directly. slab_used detects retained shared-memory
#   allocations, slab_reqs detects matched allocation/free churn that net
#   occupancy cannot see, and slab_fails detects allocator pressure. These
#   fields are rendered generically off any ngx_shm_zone_t by testkit's core
#   probe (src/ngx_test_probe.c:487-769), so they apply to this module's zone.
#   pool.cycle_cleanup is also direct: it counts cleanup handlers accidentally
#   parked on the worker-lifetime cycle pool. driver.sh's two negative controls
#   require both comparators to produce their own failure messages.
#
# WHAT THIS SCENARIO DOES NOT COVER (see ../fault-slab-store for that): the
# probe-armed slab-allocation FAULT path. This is the happy-path allocation
# shape across request size classes.

name    case 1: confirm a genuine HIT before any size-class case runs
send    GET /cached/item HTTP/1.1\r\n
send    Host: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
expect  status=200
expect  header~X-Cache: HIT
probe   fds >= 1
probe   pool.cycle_used >= 1
probe   zone.slab_reqs >= 0
delta   fds == 0
delta   pool.cycle_used == 0
delta   pool.cycle_blocks == 0
delta   pool.cycle_large == 0
delta   pool.cycle_cleanup == 0
delta   zone.slab_used == 0
delta   zone.slab_reqs <= 0
delta   zone.slab_fails == 0

name    case 2: a 30 KiB query string on the SAME cache key (still HIT)
send    GET /cached/item?
repeat  480 pad=aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa&
send     x=1 HTTP/1.1\r\n
send    Host: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
expect  status=200
expect  header~X-Cache: HIT
delta   fds == 0
delta   pool.cycle_used == 0
delta   pool.cycle_blocks == 0
delta   pool.cycle_large == 0
delta   pool.cycle_cleanup == 0
delta   zone.slab_used == 0
delta   zone.slab_reqs <= 0
delta   zone.slab_fails == 0

name    case 3: a ~96 KiB header block (two long values), still a HIT
send    GET /cached/item HTTP/1.1\r\nX-Pad-1:
repeat  800 aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
send    \r\nX-Pad-2:
repeat  800 bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb
send    \r\nHost: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
expect  status=200
expect  header~X-Cache: HIT
delta   fds == 0
delta   pool.cycle_used == 0
delta   pool.cycle_blocks == 0
delta   pool.cycle_large == 0
delta   pool.cycle_cleanup == 0
delta   zone.slab_used == 0
delta   zone.slab_reqs <= 0
delta   zone.slab_fails == 0

name    case 4: the ~96 KiB header block again, back to back
send    GET /cached/item HTTP/1.1\r\nX-Pad-1:
repeat  800 aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
send    \r\nX-Pad-2:
repeat  800 bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb
send    \r\nHost: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
expect  status=200
expect  header~X-Cache: HIT
delta   fds == 0
delta   pool.cycle_used == 0
delta   pool.cycle_blocks == 0
delta   pool.cycle_large == 0
delta   pool.cycle_cleanup == 0
delta   zone.slab_used == 0
delta   zone.slab_reqs <= 0
delta   zone.slab_fails == 0

name    case 5: a 256 KiB request body on a HIT (proxy_pass never re-reads it)
send    GET /cached/item HTTP/1.1\r\n
send    Host: prober\r\nContent-Length: 262144\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
repeat  4096 aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
expect  status=200
expect  header~X-Cache: HIT
delta   fds == 0
delta   pool.cycle_used == 0
delta   pool.cycle_blocks == 0
delta   pool.cycle_large == 0
delta   pool.cycle_cleanup == 0
delta   zone.slab_used == 0
delta   zone.slab_reqs <= 0
delta   zone.slab_fails == 0

name    case 6: tiny again, cumulative bound
send    GET /cached/item HTTP/1.1\r\n
send    Host: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
expect  status=200
expect  header~X-Cache: HIT
delta   fds == 0
delta   pool.cycle_used == 0
delta   pool.cycle_blocks == 0
delta   pool.cycle_large == 0
delta   pool.cycle_cleanup == 0
delta   zone.slab_used == 0
delta   zone.slab_reqs <= 0
delta   zone.slab_fails == 0
probe_baseline fds <= 2
probe_baseline pool.cycle_used == 0
probe_baseline pool.cycle_blocks == 0
probe_baseline pool.cycle_large == 0
probe_baseline pool.cycle_cleanup == 0
probe_baseline zone.slab_used == 0
probe_baseline zone.slab_reqs <= 0
probe_baseline zone.slab_fails == 0
